course: dictionary
lesson: 10384
title: A long trek
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trek is a long, hard journey, often on foot through mountains, forests or wild country. People go trekking in the Himalayas or the Andes. As a verb, to trek means to make that kind of journey, so they trekked for days.
explain: Trek can also be a joke about an ordinary walk. «Aw, it's a pure trek,» she groans, and she is not talking about mountains. She means the walk is very long and tiring for her. Informal speech stretches the word to make a short walk sound like an adventure.
explain: Context tells you which kind of trek is meant. Mountains and forests mean a real expedition. Groans and a shop mean a tiring walk. Swap in your meaning: "It's a long, tiring walk" still makes sense in the sentence, so you have it right.
fact: «Trek» is a noun (a trek) and a verb (to trek, trekked, trekking).
fact: «Trek» means a long, hard journey, especially on foot through mountains, forests or wild country.
fact: «Go trekking» and «pony trekking» are phrases you may hear, and «pony trekking» is a UK phrase for a journey on horseback.
fact: Informally, «trek» can mean any long, tiring walk, such as «It's a trek to the shops».
fact: In Scotland, «pure» can mean really, so «a pure trek» means a really long walk.
exercise: «People go trekking in the Himalayas.» What does trekking mean here? | A shopping trip in town | A swimming race in a lake | *A long, hard journey on foot through mountains | A quick nap on the bus
exercise: «Aw, it's a pure trek,» she groans. What does trek mean in this sentence? | A journey through wild mountains | A dance at a party | *A long tiring walk to an ordinary place
exercise: «They trekked across the valley for three days.» Find and copy the verb that means made the long journey. | three | *trekked | valley | days
test: Which phrase from the lessons means a journey on horseback in the UK? | *pony trekking | trek across | a long trek | go trekking
test: Grandad says «It's a pure trek to the bus stop.» What does he mean? | He is going on holiday | He is climbing a mountain | *He is joking that the walk is very long and tiring | He is lost in the forest
exam: Jayden reads, «The Great Trek was a migration of families across South Africa.» What does trek mean here? | A school trip to the shops | A short bus ride | *A long, hard journey by a group of people | A loud shout
